]



Then:



x_t=[s_t,c_t]



becomes the actual neural-network input.



17. What PyTorch does


The PyTorch network is essentially a function:



f_\theta(x_t)



where:




 = current state


 = learned parameters




It outputs:



[\ell_{sell},\ell_{hold},\ell_{buy}]



These are converted into probabilities:



\pi_\theta(a|x)
=
Softmax(f_\theta(x))



Example:


SELL   0.11
HOLD   0.24
BUY    0.65



The model is saying:




Given the state I've observed, BUY is currently my highest-probability action.




It is not saying:




BUY is guaranteed to make money.




That distinction is crucial.



